{#
  The site footer, previously duplicated across 8 files.

  footerMuted controls the "Response within 24 hrs" line, which had drifted to
  a 4/4 split: present on home, about, services and privacy; absent on contact,
  free-audit, blog and article. Phase 2 is a pure refactor, so each page keeps
  exactly what it had and the flag preserves the split. Phase 3 resolves it one
  way when the copy is actually reviewed.

  Contact and social details are read from _data/site.json, generated from
  branding/<client>/site.yaml by scripts/branding/build-brand.py. The social
  links come from the site.social map, so adding a network there makes it
  appear here with no template change. Note: the same contact facts still
  appear as literals elsewhere in the source (~95 occurrences); replacing those
  with these references is the remaining consolidation.
#}
{% set homeHref = "#top" if pageKey == "home" else urls.home %}
  <!-- ============ FOOTER ============ -->
  <footer class="footer on-dark">
    <div class="container footer__inner">
      <div class="footer__brand">
        <a href="{{ homeHref }}" class="footer__logo" aria-label="{{ t.common.nav.logoAria | safe }}">
          <img src="{{ site.logos.light }}" alt="{{ t.common.nav.logoAlt | safe }}" />
        </a>
{#
  What the organisation does, from the client's config — the same string a page
  falls back to for its meta description. Read like the tagline below: a locale
  key if the client declared a map, the string if they declared one line, the
  locale bundle if they declared neither.
#}
        <p>{{ site.description[locale.code] | default(site.description) | default(t.common.footer.blurb) | safe }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="footer__col">
        <h4>{{ t.common.footer.exploreHeading | safe }}</h4>
{#
  Same menu the nav renders, from src/_data/menu.js, so a section seeded in
  branding/<client>/content/ appears in both places. The blog keeps its own
  footer wording ("Insights") — the one label that differs from the nav.
#}
{% for item in menu[locale.code] %}{% set label = t.common.footer.insights if item.key == "blog" else (t.common.nav[item.labelKey] if item.labelKey else item.label) %}{% set href = homeHref if item.key == "home" else item.url %}        <a href="{{ href }}">{{ label | safe }}</a>
{% endfor %}      </div>
      <div class="footer__col">
        <h4>{{ t.common.footer.contactHeading | safe }}</h4>
{#
  Each of these used to be an anchor on a contact page — /en-ca/contact/#email —
  which meant the footer depended on that page existing. It now links to the
  thing itself: mail to the address, dial the number, go to the account. A
  client that declares none of them gets a heading and nothing under it, rather
  than links into a page that may not be there.
#}
{% if site.contact.email %}        <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact.email }}">{{ site.contact.email }}</a>
{% endif %}{% if site.contact.phoneDisplay %}        <a href="{{ site.contact.phoneHref }}">{{ site.contact.phoneDisplay }}</a>
{% endif %}{% for name, s in site.social %}        <a href="{{ s.url }}" rel="me">{{ s.label | safe }}</a>
{% endfor %}
{% if footerMuted %}        <span class="footer__muted">{{ t.common.footer.muted | safe }}</span>
{% endif %}      </div>
    </div>
{#
  The name and the tagline are the client's, so they come from site.yaml rather
  than the locale bundles — a rebrand should not mean editing translations.

  `tagline` is authored either as one string or as a map keyed by locale. Both
  are read here: the lookup wins when the key exists, the string when it does
  not, and the bundle's own tagline when the client declares neither.
#}
{% set tagline = site.tagline[locale.code] | default(site.tagline) | default(t.common.footer.tagline) %}
    <div class="container footer__bottom">
      <span>&copy; {{ buildYear }} {{ site.name | default(t.common.footer.copyright) | safe }}</span>
      <span>{{ tagline | safe }}</span>
    </div>
  </footer>
